## Tasks

- **TASK 1 — Unhead wiring.** Done. `createHead()` after pinia/router in `main.ts`; `App.vue` installs `useHead(homeSeoHead())` — the *same* builder the prerenderer writes into `dist/index.html`, so crawler and app cannot disagree. Component-scoped entry removal on unmount is **verified, not assumed**: the e2e navigates to `/plan` and asserts the title returns to `Flambette`, the canonical to `https://flambette.app/`, and that the recipe's `robots` meta and `ld+json` are *gone* (not overridden).
- **TASK 2 — RecipeDetail `useHead`.** Done. The doc loads async, so `recipeJsonLd`/`recipeSeoHead` take a **nullable** doc: every meta-derived tag (title, description, canonical, OG/Twitter) is present before the fetch resolves, and the JSON-LD upgrades itself on arrival. No "partial builder" was forked — one function, one code path, pinned by `src/lib/seo.test.ts` ("only the two doc-only JSON-LD keys are missing"). The head additionally passes `doc` only when `doc.id === meta.id` (see deviations §1).
