## Deviations from the brief (with rationale)

1. **The canonical gained a trailing slash** (`/recipe/<id>/` instead of the
   brief's `/recipe/<id>`). Reason: the prerendered page is a directory index,
   and **both** production surfaces redirect the slash-less form to the slash
   form (Cloudflare's default `html_handling: auto-trailing-slash`; nginx's
   `try_files $uri $uri/`, measured as a real 301 on the built image). The
   published form must be the one served directly, or every canonical and
   sitemap `<loc>` is a redirect. The app's own router keeps slash-less routes;
   `nginx.conf`/`wrangler.jsonc` stay untouched, as the brief requires.
2. **The prerenderer's pure core lives in `src/lib/seoRender.ts`**, not inside
   `scripts/generate-recipe-seo.ts` (which stays a thin I/O main, exactly as
   TASK 4 asked). Reason: `bun test src` globs only `src/` and
   `tsconfig.app.json` type-checks only `src/`, so a helper in `scripts/` would
   be the one piece of this feature with no test and no type coverage.
3. **`src/lib/siteUrl.ts` was added.** `DEFAULT_SITE_URL` cannot live in
   `seo.ts` and be imported by `vite.config.ts`: the config is type-checked by
   `tsconfig.node.json` (no DOM lib) and `seo.ts` reaches `images.ts`'s
   `import.meta.env`/DOM types, which fails `vue-tsc -b`.
4. **An extra e2e test and the `id="recipe-jsonld"` fix were not in the
   brief.** Found while verifying the production surface: Unhead adopts the
   static `<meta>`/`<link>` tags of a served prerendered page but an inline
   script has no identity to dedupe on, so hydration appended a **second
   identical `Recipe` object**. Both consumers now emit the shared `id`, and a
   new e2e pins "no second copy of anything" on the trailing-slash URL.
5. **`.dockerignore` was edited** (outside the brief's file list, but
   necessary). It excluded `scripts/` wholesale, so `bun run build` failed
   *inside the image* — `Module not found "scripts/generate-recipe-seo.ts"`
   after vite had already run. It now excludes only `scripts/*.py`; the
   TypeScript build step ships. Verified by building and running the image.
6. **The branch was rebased onto `origin/main`** (`138c2b9`, ADR-0040 relay
   core, landed after the brief's base `3f82c79`) and force-pushed with
   `--force-with-lease`, so the PR diff is exactly the 16 files of this work.
   The gate was re-run in full on the rebased tree (numbers above).
7. **The stale-doc guard was placed in `loadDoc()` as well as the head.**
   qodo's finding is real and reaches further than the head: without the
   guard the *view* also renders an old recipe's steps under the new
   recipe's heading. Fixing the writer and the consumer is one line each and
   keeps the invariant true at both ends.

Nothing in the brief's locked design was renegotiated: `src/lib/seo.ts` stayed
the single source, prerendering stayed head-only (plus a plain `<noscript>`
block), `SITE_URL` stayed the canonical origin, recipes stayed the only
indexable surface with the app shell canonicalizing to `/`, the JSON-LD
